    "https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2669": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Montana State University Northern Employment Opportunities | Financial Aid Specialist I, Rev. 5/11/2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help MSUN Information About MSUN About Havre Benefits Overview Academics at MSUN Quick Facts University Mission Statement on Diversity Financial Aid Specialist I, Rev. 5/11/2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In your application and required documents, DO NOT include personal protected information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. Applicants must upload the following with their application: 1. A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your career goals, and your interest in the position. 2. A resume. 3. A list of three professional references. Complete and sign the Authorization Form for Background Check Access the form here: https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation-MSU-Northern.pdf In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Financial Aid Specialist I, Rev. 5/11/2026 Brief Position Overview The Office of Financial Aid at Montana State University-Northern ( MSUN ) is seeking applications for a Financial Aid Specialist I position. Position Number 7N0001 Department Financial Aid Division Student Success Division Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Non-Exempt Union Affiliation AFSCME FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Hourly Salary $16.342-20.177 per hour Contract Type Classified Hourly If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The major purpose of this position is to provide guidance to prospective and current financial aid applicants in order to help them understand aid differences and requirements and also determine the best type(s) of aid available to them. Must be able to interpret university, state and federal rules and regulations. This position also provides guidance to prospective and current students on basic financial literacy concepts. Additionally, some data input and other tasks as assigned. Duties and Responsibilities Responsible for providing guidance to prospective and current students in order to help them understand aid differences and requirements; basic financial literacy concepts and provides technical support/assistance with the FAFSA applications including other necessary documentation that may be required. Serves as Client/Outside Agency Liaison meeting and counseling with prospective students providing information on Financial Aid procedures. Responsible for Campus Visits to students, parents, and school groups. Be familiarized and utilize the National Student Loan Database System ( NSLDS ) to advise students about their current loan debt. Provide Entrance and Exit Counseling to loan borrowers. Prepare exit packets to all withdrawing students (official and unofficial withdrawals), low enrollment, and graduating students. Participates in New Student Orientation and Registration Day providing incoming freshman with the important and appropriate information for each student notifying them of missing requirements and offer letter information. Participates and assists in coordination of the New/Continuing Student Scholarship application process and the Scholarship Ceremony. Record and input scholarships on student’s accounts as well as other data input as needed for the office. Process financial aid forms and assist in the offer letter process. Ensure scholarship eligibility for the Merit Scholarship and Chancellor Scholarship as well as other MSUN Scholarships. Maintain and manage Financial Aid Live Support Chat, Financial Aid webpage, forms and publications such as Consumer Information for prospective and current students. Answer phones, order supplies for the office and backup the front desk duties as needed. Responsible for providing support on procedures and processes for Specialist II as needed. List any secondary duties assigned to this position: 1. Contribute to general customer service in Student Central 2. Serve on university committees as appropriate. 3. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Associate Degree in Business, Education, or related field; OR significant work experience in customer relations, in business, in finance or banking, or in higher education offices. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Demonstrated experience working with students in an education setting. Demonstrated financial literacy skills (budgeting, career earnings, loans). Demonstrated experience working in higher education. Computer experience including Microsoft Office. Demonstrated experience in handling sensitive and confidential situations and information. Demonstrated ability to work independently. The Successful Candidate Will Communicate effectively in both written and verbal with a variety of ages and backgrounds. Someone who can process and learn information in a timely manner Motivated and attention to detail. Special Requirements Physical Demands Ability to work with or without reasonable accommodations in a typical office environment Ability to lift up to 30 pounds. This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 2600020P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Immediate Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Until an adequate pool is established No Special Instructions Summary In your application and required documents, DO NOT include personal protected information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. Applicants must upload the following with their application: 1. A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your career goals, and your interest in the position. 2. A resume. 3. A list of three professional references. Complete and sign the Authorization Form for Background Check Access the form here: https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation- MSU -Northern.pdf In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2662 EEOC Statement Montana State University-Northern ( MSUN ) is an equal opportunity employer. MSUN does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSUN provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Director of Human Resources /Title IX Montana State University-Northern 300 11th Street West Havre, MT 59501 E-mail: rebecca.farr@msun.edu Location: 208 Cowan Hall Tel: (406) 265.3568 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © Montana State University Northern Accessibility Admissions Administration Contact List Jobs Privacy Policy Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
