    "https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2687": {
      "title": "Recruiting Specialist",
      "description": "Montana State University Northern Employment Opportunities | Recruiting Specialist Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help MSUN Information About MSUN About Havre Benefits Overview Academics at MSUN Quick Facts University Mission Statement on Diversity Recruiting Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In this application, and the required cover letter, resume, and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation-MSU-Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Recruiting Specialist Brief Position Overview The Office of Recruiting at Montana State University-Northern ( MSUN ) seeks applications for their Recruiting Specialist position. This full-time Professional position is on a 12-month contract following the fiscal year and eligible for MUS Benefits. Position Number 7C0048 Department Recruiting Division Appointment Type Professional Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Exempt Union Affiliation FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Annual Salary $45,200 annually Contract Type MUS If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Office of Recruiting at Montana State University-Northern connects prospective students and their families with the opportunities available at MSU -Northern through campus visits, community outreach, presentations, individualized guidance, and recruitment activities across Montana and beyond. Every day is different, offering opportunities to build relationships, tell the university’s story, and help students find a place where they can succeed. Duties and Responsibilities Key duties including, but not limited to the following: Student Recruitment and Engagement Maintain current knowledge of university academic programs and admissions standards Provide correct and appropriate information to prospective students and serve as a central point of contact for students and their families Build relationships with prospective students, high school counselors, teachers, and others through events, as well as face-to-face, phone, email, text, mail, and other communications Represent MSU -Northern through campus visits, school visits, college fairs, community events, and informational presentations to prospective students, families, and other audiences Provide campus tours and assist prospective students through the application and admission process Assist with on-campus events and represent MSU -Northern at university and community events Assist with the coordination and daily support of the Student Ambassador Program Recruitment Travel and Outreach Travel extensively (approximately 25 weeks annually), including in-state, out-of-state, and international destinations Records, Systems, and Administrative Support Enter and maintain data accurately and in accordance with data security and privacy standards Use Customer Relationship Management ( CRM ) software for student contact management, communication, and outreach efforts Collaboration and Institutional Service Collaborate effectively with colleagues to accomplish departmental goals Collaborate with other departments to stay current on academic programs, policies, procedures, and student activities Contribute to the overall customer service function of Student Central Serve on institutional committees as requested Perform other duties as assigned to support the mission and goals of the institution Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Bachelor’s degree, or Associate’s degree plus relevant work experience demonstrating excellent communication skills Current and valid Montana driver’s license or the ability to obtain one within a month of hire Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience working with students in admissions, recruiting, residence life, student government, orientation, academic support, or other campus organizations Knowledge or experience using Anthology Reach or a similar CRM Knowledge or experience using Banner or similar database Experience planning and coordinating projects and events Demonstrated excellent customer service experience Demonstrated excellent oral and written communications skills Sales experience The Successful Candidate Will Outstanding organizational and communication skills Comfort communicating with individuals and groups in a variety of settings Ability to develop and maintain relationships with key partners Commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion Team-first attitude Self-motivation and initiative Willingness to travel and work evenings/weekends as needed Ability to handle confidential information with attention to detail Ability to multi-task and solve problems innovativel Ability to represent the university professionally Strong time management skills Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and related software Special Requirements Physical Demands The ability to perform the following with or without reasonable accommodations: 1. Lift up to 50 pounds 2. Travel extensively 3. Work in a typical office environment This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 2700003P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date Immediate Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Until an adequate pool is established No Special Instructions Summary In this application, and the required cover letter, resume, and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation- MSU -Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2686 EEOC Statement Montana State University-Northern ( MSUN ) is an equal opportunity employer. MSUN does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSUN provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Director of Human Resources /Title IX Montana State University-Northern 300 11th Street West Havre, MT 59501 E-mail: rebecca.farr@msun.edu Location: 208 Cowan Hall Tel: (406) 265.3568 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © Montana State University Northern Accessibility Admissions Administration Contact List Jobs Privacy Policy Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2696": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Montana State University Northern Employment Opportunities | Culinary Professional II/Cook II Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help MSUN Information About MSUN About Havre Benefits Overview Academics at MSUN Quick Facts University Mission Statement on Diversity Culinary Professional II/Cook II Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In this application, and the required cover letter and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume or curriculum vitae. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation-MSU-Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Position Details Position Information NBAPOSN Title Working Title Culinary Professional II/Cook II Brief Position Overview Position Number TBD Department Food Services Division Office of Food Services Appointment Type Classified Contract Term Fiscal Year Semester If other, specify From date If other, specify End date FLSA Non-Exempt Union Affiliation AFSCME FTE 1.0 Benefits Eligible Yes Compensation Hourly Salary $17.55 per hour Contract Type Classified Hourly If other, please specify Recruitment Type Open Position Details General Statement The Culinary Professional II position has responsibility to prepare, cook, and serve a variety of foods, primarily in large quantities for student, campus, and community consumption. Culinary Professional II staff are expected to exemplify high levels of customer service and attention to detail, as they work to fulfill the dietary needs for a vibrant and engaged campus community. This position will take orders from patrons and serve patrons at counters or tables. Culinary Professional II staff may supervise student staff during weekend and evening operations. Additionally, Culinary Professional II staff provide support to Retail & Finance staff in Dining Services. Duties and Responsibilities Take orders, interact with customers, prepare, cook, and serve food in large quantities and, at times, over short periods of time or in response to individual requests. Prepare food according to recipe, taking care to ensure the efficient use of resources and the communication of needs in a timely and effective fashion. Ensure high levels of customer service, both in interactions with patrons and in presentation of food and dining environment. Perform a variety of food preparation and operational tasks, to include making sandwiches, carving meats, making soups and salads, brewing coffee, and suggesting adjustments to recipes, ordering processes, and overall enhancements where appropriate. Supervise and train student workers. Assist with ordering and inventory as requested. Develop, test, and refine new recipes and menu items. Perform general cleaning activities in kitchen and dining areas, to include cleaning food preparation equipment, work areas, and counters or tables. Assist with Catering Events when needed. Required Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills 1. High School diploma or equivalent. 2. Knowledge of basic food safety standards. 3. Customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications – Experience, Education, Knowledge & Skills Experience in food service. Management or supervisor experience. The Successful Candidate Will 1. Ability to follow a recipe. 2. Ability to “plate” meals for a nice presentation. 3. Ability to allow for a flexible work schedule if changes should arise. Special Requirements Physical Demands The ability to work with or without reasonable accommodations in a position where the following are part of the work: prolonged standing, extreme temperature changes, lifting items up to 30 lbs, multi-tasking, constant interruptions. This position has supervisory duties? No Posting Detail Information Announcement Number STAFF - VA - 2700002P Number of Vacancies 3 Desired Start Date Immediate Position End Date (if temporary) Open Date Close Date Until an adequate pool is established No Special Instructions Summary In this application, and the required cover letter and list of references, DO NOT include your protected private information such as date of birth, citizenship status or immigration information, social security number, or any other protected information. This does not apply to the Authorization Form for Background Check. Applicants must upload the following with their application: A cover letter which addresses how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, your professional and academic career goals, and your interest in the position. A resume or curriculum vitae. A list of three professional references. In the online application in the Background Check field, type YES to show you understand this additional requirement. Complete an Authorization Form for Background Check https://www.msun.edu/hr/forms/Authorization_for_Background_Investigation- MSU -Northern.pdf Submit your completed and signed form to: Human Resources Montana State University-Northern P.O. Box 7751 Havre, MT 59501-7751 406-265-3568 or 406-265-3789 HR Dept. Fax 406-265-3530 Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.msun.edu/postings/2684 EEOC Statement Montana State University-Northern ( MSUN ) is an equal opportunity employer. MSUN does not discriminate against any applicant on the basis of race, color, religion, creed, political ideas, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, marital status, national origin, physical or mental disability, or any other protected class status in violation of any applicable law. In compliance with the Montana Veteran’s Employment Preference Act, MSUN provides preference in employment to veterans, disabled veterans, and certain eligible relatives of veterans. To claim veteran’s preference, please complete the veteran’s preference information located in the Demographics section of your profile. Director of Human Resources /Title IX Montana State University-Northern 300 11th Street West Havre, MT 59501 E-mail: rebecca.farr@msun.edu Location: 208 Cowan Hall Tel: (406) 265.3568 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). © Montana State University Northern Accessibility Admissions Administration Contact List Jobs Privacy Policy Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
